# Citation for StreamBridge.
#
# Cite this work with the metadata below. If you fork or extend StreamBridge,
# update the authors and the version to match your own work: a citation that
# points at someone else's repository for a change you made is worse than no
# citation at all.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "StreamBridge: a local streaming bridge between online music sources and MPD"
abstract: >-
  StreamBridge is a local HTTP bridge that makes an online music catalogue
  playable in MPD, and therefore in any MPD client. It resolves sources on
  demand, serves them over a loopback-only HTTP endpoint, and never stores
  audio, sends telemetry, or requires an account. It ships a browser interface,
  a command line client, and a machine-readable HTTP API.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/streambridge"
url: "https://github.com/OWNER/streambridge"
keywords:
  - music
  - mpd
  - streaming
  - self-hosted
  - privacy
authors:
  - name: "StreamBridge contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/OWNER/streambridge/graphs/contributors"
